# novadeck build-provenance markers — paths that must NEVER reach a shipped root.
#
# One tree-relative path per line (no leading /); blank lines and #-comments ignored.
# images/guard-rootfs.sh asserts every line is absent from the staged tree before an image is
# built from it.
#
# ASSERTION ONLY (Phase 4c). This file used to be half of a declare/apply/assert triple: the
# root was `docker export` of a vendor-built container image, so it arrived carrying artifacts
# of two build systems that were not ours, images/assemble-rootfs.sh removed every line here,
# and the guard then checked the removal. The root is now bootstrapped from packages —
# `pacman -r <empty-dir>` in images/customize-base.sh — so no container filesystem contributes
# bytes to it, nothing has to be removed, and the scrub is gone. The `optional` flag went with
# it: it only ever suppressed the scrub's not-found report, and there is no longer a tree in
# which a marker is expected to be present.
#
# The declaration stays because the asymmetry that justified it has not changed: a marker that
# reaches a device costs a hardware debug cycle to find and shows no build-time symptom, while
# checking for one costs a stat. It is now a REGRESSION guard — if anything ever reintroduces a
# container filesystem as a content source, this fails the build instead of the device.
#
# Two entries the audit found are NOT listed any more, because they cannot occur in a tree no
# vendor image contributed to: `repos` and `etc/mash-ci-tracking.job_id`, both artifacts of the
# base image's own CI pipeline (found 2026-07-26 by an unowned-file sweep of the pinned base:
# 31,203 files, 30,012 owned by a package; both were reaching the image).

# --- container runtimes -------------------------------------------------------------------
# `systemd-detect-virt` reports a container when these exist, and systemd then SILENTLY skips
# every ConditionVirtualization=!container unit — ~13 of them, systemd-timesyncd being the
# visible casualty (clock stuck at epoch). HW-confirmed 2026-06-25, back when `docker export`
# baked /.dockerenv straight into the root.
.dockerenv
run/.containerenv
